<div class="mt-4 mx-auto" style="max-width: 52em;">
    <h2 class="mb-2">Person Centered Planning Is Here!</h2>
    <p>PC2 is excited to announce that we are now offering Facilitated Person Centered Planning.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-4 mb-2">What Is Person Centered Planning?</h2>
    <p>
        Person Centered Planning is a process of planning that is driven by the individual and is rooted in
        community and not a service system. Although services are very much a part of the picture, they are
        not the driving force or vision. As a result, person centered planning is an evolving picture of a
        persons strengths, skills, dreams and goals that provide a roadmap to the future in work, school,
        home, relationships and community life.
    </p>
    <p>
        Person Centered Planning allows an individual to create a path to having the life that they want and
        the ability to have control over their own life decisions.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-4 mb-2">How It Works</h2>
    <p>
        Using a process called MAPPING, an individual and their team of family, friends, teachers, service
        providers and others, share information to build their Person Centered Plan.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-4 mb-2">What&rsquo;s Included in a PCP?</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>A Path to Action Plans centered on the person&rsquo;s talents, hopes and dreams</li>
        <li>A facilitated process focusing on key questions and themes such as &ldquo;who am I?&rdquo;, &ldquo;what are my goals?&rdquo;, &ldquo;what are my dreams?&rdquo;</li>
        <li>Inviting people who are a part of the individuals life. Family members, friends, teachers, service providers, neighbors, and anyone else that can help with the process.</li>
        <li>Graphic recording - pictures and words for all abilities to honor the whole person.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

